      "content": "Most AI safety tooling inspects single prompt-response pairs, missing malicious patterns that span multiple tool invocations. A single tool call to read a file or ping an endpoint looks completely benign in isolation, yet the sequence of reading private keys followed by outbound network access constitutes exfiltration.\n\nCisco designed Project Quarry around a neurosymbolic approach: compiling declarative behavioral rules directly into finite state machines. By modeling valid and invalid agent execution graphs, the engine enforces strict ordering constraints over transcripts. For example, reading a local secret and subsequently calling an external HTTP endpoint triggers a violation, whereas reversing the order does not.\n\nFor engineers running production coding agents, this model provides transparent and deterministic auditing over JSON execution traces without incurring the latency and hallucination risks of putting an LLM judge on every single turn."
    },
    {
